WEBVTT

00:09.426 --> 00:12.262
Ugh. If I'm ever in a coma,
put braces on my teeth.

00:12.346 --> 00:13.931
- Okay.
- Thanks, buddy.

00:14.014 --> 00:15.349
Oh, thank you.

00:16.016 --> 00:18.310
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:18.393 --> 00:21.271
Wait, that's your secret smile.
You've got a little secret.

00:21.355 --> 00:23.857
It's... It's nothing really. It's...

00:23.941 --> 00:25.108
Tell us!

00:26.068 --> 00:28.612
My sister wants my sperm.

00:28.695 --> 00:29.696
Oh.

00:30.697 --> 00:32.491
Context? Any context would be lovely.

00:32.574 --> 00:34.618
- Explain, please.
- Right, yes. Okay, scooch.

00:34.701 --> 00:36.787
- So... my mom and I are on the phone, right?
- Uh-huh.

00:36.870 --> 00:39.289
I'm telling her I'm hungry,
she's listing off foods I can eat.

00:39.373 --> 00:40.707
And suddenly she tells me

00:40.791 --> 00:43.544
that my sister Talia and her wife
are thinking about having a baby.

00:43.627 --> 00:44.878
- Oh, my--
- Wait, wait.

00:44.962 --> 00:46.421
And then out of the blue,

00:46.505 --> 00:50.425
Talia texts me saying she wants
to stop by the house next week.

00:51.051 --> 00:53.553
I mean, she's after my seed, ultimately.

00:53.637 --> 00:56.640
Oh, my God.
First baby of the friend group.

00:56.723 --> 00:59.142
- That's wild.
- Look, it's not that big of a deal.

00:59.226 --> 01:03.563
This is just what happens when two little
gay siblings become two big gay grown-ups.

01:03.647 --> 01:07.192
I mean, you have to assume one might ask
the other for genetic material.

01:09.403 --> 01:11.822
What? Why this? Why the silence?

01:11.905 --> 01:16.410
No, nothing. I just... I didn't realize
that you had that kind of relationship.

01:16.493 --> 01:18.203
You're famously a monster
around your big sister.

01:18.287 --> 01:20.163
- Yeah, that.
- I mean, yes.

01:20.247 --> 01:24.084
Have I historically been something
of a drain to Talia? Sure.

01:24.668 --> 01:28.755
But does it feel so good
to finally be seen as a faucet? It does.

01:28.839 --> 01:31.300
Like a faucet in a few ways.

01:31.383 --> 01:33.176
Can I just ask the thing?

01:33.260 --> 01:36.471
No, Samir, it's not incest, okay?
Her wife would be carrying the baby.

01:36.555 --> 01:37.889
No, I was...

01:37.973 --> 01:41.518
- gonna ask if you feel nervous.
- Aw.

01:42.185 --> 01:43.186
A little bit.

01:43.270 --> 01:44.980
But mostly, I'm excited.

01:45.689 --> 01:46.982
- And honored.
- Mm-hmm.

01:47.524 --> 01:49.651
And ready. Oh, I'm ready.

01:49.735 --> 01:51.903
Can you believe it?

01:51.987 --> 01:52.988
Such a good retcon.

01:53.071 --> 01:54.948
I was totally gonna ask the incest thing.

01:55.032 --> 01:56.908
I was right there with you, brother. Yeah.

02:02.205 --> 02:04.458
♪ I need some bad advice ♪

02:07.627 --> 02:09.629
♪ Stay up tonight ♪

02:10.714 --> 02:12.716
♪ We'll make it out alive ♪

02:16.094 --> 02:20.265
Your egg freezing kit includes FSH,
trigger shot...

02:21.975 --> 02:24.102
- Gonadotropin. Where is it?
- Wow.

02:24.186 --> 02:25.896
I did not know
you were so serious about this.

02:25.979 --> 02:29.274
Yeah, Anton becoming an uncle-father
made me take a good hard look

02:29.358 --> 02:30.817
at my own fertility.

02:30.901 --> 02:33.111
- Like, I'm an only child.
- No. You?

02:33.195 --> 02:36.156
Which made me special,
but ultimately lonely.

02:36.239 --> 02:38.158
So I want five kids.

02:38.241 --> 02:40.118
Which means
I got to throw some eggs on ice.

02:40.202 --> 02:42.704
Iss, please let me know
if I can help with any of this.

02:42.788 --> 02:44.581
- Okay?
- Thank you.

02:44.665 --> 02:47.751
- You know what they say about fertility.
- No, what?

02:49.294 --> 02:51.922
- I don't know, like, specifically.
- Oh.

02:52.464 --> 02:55.717
- Okay, I am off.
- Wow, there she is.

02:55.801 --> 02:58.261
Juror number four in the courts
but number one in our hearts.

02:58.345 --> 03:01.264
Thanks. Yeah, I don't know why people
complain about jury duty so much.

03:01.348 --> 03:02.474
It's really not that bad.

03:02.557 --> 03:05.102
- And by that you mean...
- I'm having the best week of my life.

03:05.185 --> 03:06.520
- There it is.
- Yep.

03:06.603 --> 03:07.729
God, all this time looking for a job

03:07.813 --> 03:09.898
and then one comes along
mandated by the state.

03:09.981 --> 03:13.318
I have routine. I have structure.
I have a judge who sees me as a daughter.

03:13.402 --> 03:15.821
I'm sorry I can't help you
with your egg freezing this week.

03:15.904 --> 03:18.073
Oh, my God, it's okay.
My ovaries know you care.

03:18.156 --> 03:19.866
That's for me. I've got it.

03:19.950 --> 03:22.953
I'm getting it. That's for me.
I'm getting it. Excuse me! Whoo!

03:23.662 --> 03:24.830
- Hi!
- Hi!

03:24.913 --> 03:27.707
You guys, my big sister's here.

03:30.210 --> 03:31.378
What the fuck is that?

03:31.461 --> 03:33.880
Wow, crown moldings?

03:33.964 --> 03:35.674
- Prince in a palace.
- I know.

03:35.757 --> 03:37.843
My face is on the currency.
I look regal but stern.

03:37.926 --> 03:39.553
Like, mm-mmm.

03:40.595 --> 03:43.014
Okay, okay. Couch or chairs?
How do you picture it?

03:43.098 --> 03:44.891
We could do the couch.
I'm not gonna be here that long.

03:44.975 --> 03:47.602
Great, couch.
I can really see it on the couch.

03:51.314 --> 03:53.150
So...

03:53.900 --> 03:55.068
Do you want to start, or should I?

03:55.152 --> 03:57.279
- I don't know how this works.
- I could start. Yeah.

03:57.362 --> 04:01.783
Okay, so you left this
at Mom and Dad's house, so take that.

04:02.576 --> 04:05.454
- Okay.
- Oh. Mom wanted me to give you this.

04:05.537 --> 04:07.330
She says you need
to drink some more water.

04:07.414 --> 04:10.876
She's worried that you're only drinking
juice and you'll be dead by 40. Okay?

04:10.959 --> 04:12.169
- Okay.
- Good.

04:13.336 --> 04:14.421
And...

04:14.504 --> 04:16.673
Yes?

04:16.756 --> 04:20.760
I need you to sign this card for Nana
and Pop-pop 'cause it's their anniversary.

04:20.844 --> 04:22.637
All right? So here, sign your name.

04:22.721 --> 04:24.806
Big boy handwriting. Thank you, sir.

04:25.682 --> 04:27.476
Great, and signed for you.

04:27.559 --> 04:28.727
Thank you.

04:29.311 --> 04:33.315
And anything from me that you might need?

04:33.940 --> 04:35.066
Like what?

04:35.150 --> 04:38.111
Come on. Talia.

04:38.195 --> 04:39.529
Anton. What?

04:39.613 --> 04:41.656
Okay, okay.

04:43.742 --> 04:44.993
You can have my sperm.

04:46.703 --> 04:48.580
Wh...

04:52.542 --> 04:53.543
I know.

04:53.627 --> 04:56.546
It's the gift of life.
There is no right way to react to it.

04:56.630 --> 04:58.632
What are you talking about?

04:59.925 --> 05:01.009
What?

05:01.092 --> 05:03.762
Because Mom said you
and Brooke were trying to have a baby.

05:03.845 --> 05:08.266
Yeah but, like, I'm not gonna let the kid
that ruined every family vacation

05:08.350 --> 05:11.478
father my child.

05:12.354 --> 05:14.606
I mean, you left your jacket
at Mommy and Daddy's house.

05:14.689 --> 05:17.609
Okay. First of all,
it was Mom's car, actually.

05:17.692 --> 05:19.569
And you ruined Puerto Vallarta.

05:19.653 --> 05:22.322
- You got your period on the banana boat.
- All right, we're done here.

05:22.405 --> 05:23.949
- I'm gonna leave.
- Bye.

05:24.032 --> 05:25.992
- What do you want me to do with this?
- I don't want that.

05:26.076 --> 05:27.911
Fine, you probably don't even know
how to use it anyway.

05:27.994 --> 05:30.747
- Fine, I'll keep it.
- If you insist. Okay.

05:30.831 --> 05:34.209
Opposite trick. You just used
the opposite trick on me, Talia.

05:34.292 --> 05:36.795
- You're still doing the opposite trick.
- I didn't, Anton.

05:36.878 --> 05:39.714
You did. Keep the Brita. Okay?
We don't have space to plug it in anyways.

05:39.798 --> 05:41.675
Plug it in? Bro.

05:41.758 --> 05:43.677
It goes in the fridge.

05:43.760 --> 05:46.471
It's a figure of speech, Talia!

05:47.514 --> 05:49.975
That's a figure of speech.
You don't know slang.

05:54.646 --> 05:56.064
- Hey, baby.
- Mom.

05:56.147 --> 05:58.275
- How'd it go?
- He's a disaster.

05:58.358 --> 06:00.110
No, he's a full-on disaster.

06:02.904 --> 06:04.739
Oh.

06:05.532 --> 06:06.867
- Hey, Iss.
- Hey.

06:06.950 --> 06:08.577
Do you need any help with that?

06:09.202 --> 06:11.663
Oh, I mean If you're not doing
anything today, yeah, sure.

06:11.746 --> 06:13.790
- Yeah.
- Yeah, I just need to jab this,

06:13.874 --> 06:18.461
um... [clears throat] ...into here, but, uh...

06:18.545 --> 06:19.838
I'm scared.

06:19.921 --> 06:21.673
- All right.
- This feels huge.

06:21.756 --> 06:23.633
I'm just a child. Samir. Like...

06:24.676 --> 06:27.095
- What if I strike the core?
- Hey. It's okay.

06:28.263 --> 06:30.307
- Do you want me to try?
- Yes, thank you.

06:30.390 --> 06:33.393
Just know whatever I say while you're
doing it, like, I don't mean any of it.

06:33.476 --> 06:35.020
Yeah. It's fine.

06:35.854 --> 06:37.689
Fuck you, you're gonna die!

06:37.772 --> 06:40.942
You're a bitch! You're a loser incel,
fucking eunuch, you bitch!

06:44.446 --> 06:46.656
- Let's try something else.
- Yeah, that sounds good. Okay.

06:47.157 --> 06:48.700
Here we go.

06:48.783 --> 06:50.076
Sorry, go again.

06:51.286 --> 06:52.287
Sorry, go again.

06:52.370 --> 06:55.457
- Run at it. Run at it!
- Okay!

06:55.540 --> 06:57.917
Okay, I'm ready. Samir?

06:58.001 --> 07:00.211
- Here comes the airplane.
- Don't do that.

07:00.295 --> 07:03.214
Just throw it at me.
Throw... [yelps] ...You missed.

07:03.298 --> 07:04.799
- Oh, my God.
- What?

07:05.508 --> 07:07.552
- Back up into it.
- I can't, I can't, I can't.

07:09.888 --> 07:11.806
Oh, my God. What is that?

07:14.934 --> 07:16.519
Nice.

07:16.603 --> 07:18.021
- What the hell?
- Right?

07:19.064 --> 07:20.607
Oh, my God, wait.

07:20.690 --> 07:22.901
- Same time tomorrow?
- Same time tomorrow.

07:30.075 --> 07:31.868
Iss, you don't mind
that I'm not helping?

07:31.951 --> 07:33.286
No, it's actually great.

07:33.370 --> 07:35.872
Freezing your eggs is so vulnerable.

07:35.955 --> 07:37.207
You're, like, hormonal.

07:37.290 --> 07:39.584
Someone has to pinch
your belly fat every day.

07:39.668 --> 07:43.880
So I needed someone that I could never,
ever feel any sexual attraction towards.

07:43.963 --> 07:45.382
And that's why I chose Samir.

07:45.465 --> 07:46.591
I'm a caretaker now.

07:46.675 --> 07:49.469
- Carly says it's very becoming of me.
- Aw.

07:49.552 --> 07:51.513
You can use "becoming" like that.
Did you know that?

07:51.596 --> 07:53.640
Okay, well, I'm glad
your fertility journey's going well.

07:53.723 --> 07:56.142
- 'Cause mine has been so bad.
- Sweetie.

07:56.226 --> 07:58.103
I mean,
Talia has no interest in having my child.

07:58.186 --> 08:00.271
Can you believe that?
She literally laughed in my face.

08:00.355 --> 08:03.483
So, Anton? Some of us are never gonna have
kids with our sisters.

08:03.566 --> 08:04.818
Is that really the worst thing?

08:04.901 --> 08:06.986
Okay, but this isn't actually
about the kid, right?

08:07.070 --> 08:08.738
It's, like, what the kid represents.

08:08.822 --> 08:10.657
Yes, this is about how my sister sees me.

08:10.740 --> 08:15.328
Which is so far from the charming,
well adjusted person I've become.

08:15.412 --> 08:16.746
Oh.

08:16.830 --> 08:18.123
Regular or premium?

08:18.206 --> 08:20.417
Ugh. What would you do, a splash of both?

08:20.500 --> 08:22.919
I'm kidding.
We'll just take regular, please.

08:23.002 --> 08:24.379
- Thank you. Yeah.
- Regular it is.

08:24.462 --> 08:27.757
See? That's the charming Anton
that we know.

08:27.841 --> 08:29.551
Oh, one second. Sorry.

08:29.634 --> 08:30.802
Hi, sweetie.

08:30.885 --> 08:34.180
What the hell is wrong with you, Mom?
You made me look like an idiot!

08:34.264 --> 08:35.932
What are you talking about?
What did I do this time?

08:36.015 --> 08:38.268
I'm talking about your daughter,
who you raised.

08:38.351 --> 08:41.187
Why would you raise someone like that?
I'm just curious. Why would you do that?

08:41.271 --> 08:43.732
- Whoa.
- We know, yeah.

08:43.815 --> 08:46.484
So he's a delight
to all seven billion people on this earth

08:46.568 --> 08:48.403
except the three he's related to.

08:48.486 --> 08:49.487
Call her, Mom, okay?

08:49.571 --> 08:51.781
Tell her to take my sperm.
Tell her she has to.

08:52.490 --> 08:53.658
There he is.

08:53.742 --> 08:55.785
- There you go.
- Oh, thank you, thank you, thank you.

08:55.869 --> 08:57.787
- You're a dream.
- Me?

08:57.871 --> 08:59.914
No, not you, Mom.
You're a fucking nightmare!

08:59.998 --> 09:02.333
- Hey, hey, Anton, I think we should--
- Mom, Mom,

09:02.417 --> 09:05.170
if you don't fix this,
I will never speak to you again, okay?

09:05.253 --> 09:09.215
We will only communicate through Dad,
and we both know he cannot convey tone.

09:09.299 --> 09:11.176
I gotta walk the dog. I'll call you back.

09:11.259 --> 09:13.261
'Kay. Say hi to Dad. Love you.

09:14.846 --> 09:16.765
Oh.

09:18.767 --> 09:20.310
Guys, I'm gonna say it.

09:20.393 --> 09:22.520
I think this has been
the best day of the trial yet.

09:22.604 --> 09:26.066
Like, everyone is just,
like, bop-bop-bop, on fire.

09:26.149 --> 09:27.150
- Yeah.
- Totally.

09:27.233 --> 09:30.820
Hey, Rodney, be honest,
are we the best jury you've ever seen?

09:32.155 --> 09:36.284
Oh. We got him.
He's smiling. He's smiling.

09:36.367 --> 09:39.496
Oh, uh, guys, that reminds me,
did everyone join the group chat?

09:39.579 --> 09:40.580
- I did.
- I did.

09:40.663 --> 09:43.208
FYI, I didn't include the alternates
in the group chat.

09:43.291 --> 09:44.959
They are alternates for a reason.

09:47.378 --> 09:48.671
Should that go on the board?

09:48.755 --> 09:50.590
Board, board, board, board!

09:50.673 --> 09:52.050
Okay, put it on the board.

09:54.719 --> 09:57.263
- Ugh, Is Billie home yet?
- No.

09:57.347 --> 09:59.682
Where is she? Oh, my God.
She left the kitchen a mess.

09:59.766 --> 10:03.812
- Hey, Ant, so, earlier with your mom...
- Ugh. I know, I know.

10:03.895 --> 10:06.439
- We bicker.
- No, that was not bickering.

10:06.523 --> 10:09.025
That was like a whole other guy
I've never met before.

10:09.692 --> 10:11.694
- Ok-Okay.
- I'm gonna be honest with you.

10:11.778 --> 10:14.280
Your sister is not going to want
to have a baby with that guy.

10:14.364 --> 10:15.448
That was not...

10:15.532 --> 10:17.784
sperm-worthy.

10:18.743 --> 10:20.286
It's just... It's hard.

10:20.370 --> 10:23.540
My family sees me a certain way
and then I act a certain way,

10:23.623 --> 10:25.500
and then they see me that way more.

10:25.583 --> 10:26.960
The cycle, it's vicious.

10:27.043 --> 10:29.254
No, dude, I get that.
That's family, right?

10:29.337 --> 10:32.090
But we got to show Talia
the person that you are now.

10:32.173 --> 10:34.425
- You're the most mature of any of us.
- No, no, no.

10:34.509 --> 10:36.970
- You have TSA PreCheck.
- No, Global Entry.

10:37.053 --> 10:38.721
You have a Wordle streak, for fuck's sake.

10:38.805 --> 10:40.640
Yeah, and I'm actually diving
into Connections.

10:40.723 --> 10:42.392
- You're diving in!
- Yeah, I'm dabbling now.

10:42.475 --> 10:45.103
Okay, so let's show her that guy, right?
And I can help you.

10:45.770 --> 10:48.439
- Really?
- Oh, yeah. I'm the sister whisperer.

10:48.523 --> 10:51.693
My sister Blair Baker and I
have only ever fought once ever.

10:51.776 --> 10:52.986
It was over Cheez-Its.

10:53.069 --> 10:54.904
We said sorry for weeks.

10:55.488 --> 10:56.739
I mean, sure, if you want to.

10:56.823 --> 10:59.033
Hey, are you guys hungry?

10:59.117 --> 11:01.244
- Oh, my God.
- Hey, Samy, wait!

11:01.327 --> 11:05.290
No! You're balding, you're short, you're
a loser, you live in your mom's house!

11:07.625 --> 11:09.419
- Nice.
- Oh.

11:09.502 --> 11:11.963
- Best one yet? Yeah! [chuckles] Whoo!
- Right?

11:17.802 --> 11:19.762
Hell of a day. Hell of a day.

11:19.846 --> 11:21.055
Ladies and gentlemen.

11:21.139 --> 11:24.017
- Rodney.
- The judge would like a word.

11:24.100 --> 11:26.144
Oh, my God, I bet we're being sequestered.

11:27.353 --> 11:29.898
The bailiff has brought something
to my attention.

11:29.981 --> 11:33.902
Who here sent baked goods to all
the litigants and their legal teams?

11:33.985 --> 11:35.069
Oh, my God.

11:35.153 --> 11:38.573
In all my years on the bench,
I've never seen anything like this.

11:38.656 --> 11:40.283
No, you have not.

11:40.366 --> 11:41.701
Who did this?

11:41.784 --> 11:44.412
Because whoever did
just caused a mistrial.

11:45.163 --> 11:46.581
- What?
- Mistrial?

11:46.664 --> 11:49.500
What? A mistrial?

11:49.584 --> 11:51.711
Goddamn it. Who was it? Admit it.

11:52.503 --> 11:55.006
Guys, admit it. If it was you, admit it.

11:55.089 --> 11:56.257
Juror number four?

11:57.342 --> 11:58.718
Oh, my God?

12:01.012 --> 12:02.305
Underneath her seat.

12:02.388 --> 12:04.432
Between our seats,
but mostly under her seat.

12:04.515 --> 12:05.600
I can't believe this.

12:05.683 --> 12:06.935
Juror number four.

12:10.146 --> 12:12.398
Can I please be considered
for the retrial?

12:14.400 --> 12:16.527
Do you think we have
enough candles?

12:16.611 --> 12:19.656
Like, does it look candlelit
or just lit by candles?

12:19.739 --> 12:21.699
Okay, Anton. Hey, Ant, look at me.

12:21.783 --> 12:23.326
Breathe, okay?

12:23.409 --> 12:26.371
You are a grown up and Talia's gonna see
what the rest of us see.

12:26.454 --> 12:27.830
- Okay.
- Trust me, after tonight,

12:27.914 --> 12:30.416
your sister's gonna be begging
for your sperm.

12:31.292 --> 12:33.753
- Okay?
- Okay, you're right. You're right.

12:33.836 --> 12:34.921
They're here.

12:35.004 --> 12:36.881
Okay, okay.

12:36.965 --> 12:38.299
They're here.

12:38.883 --> 12:40.802
Wow, this is quite a fancy...

12:40.885 --> 12:42.428
what is it, a diner?

12:42.512 --> 12:45.181
- Well, we did the place up.
- Stop it.

12:45.265 --> 12:46.933
Just for you.

12:47.016 --> 12:49.143
Uh, bro? We good?

12:49.227 --> 12:50.353
Because of yesterday?

12:50.436 --> 12:52.438
Oh, water, bridge. We're here.

12:52.522 --> 12:54.315
- Okay. Good. I love that.
- Great.

12:54.399 --> 12:56.526
And you must be Brooke. What a pleasure.

12:56.609 --> 12:59.028
- I'm so sorry. You are?
- I'm Paul Baker.

12:59.112 --> 13:00.571
I'm your maître d' this fine evening.

13:00.655 --> 13:02.031
- Ooh la la.
- Right?

13:04.492 --> 13:06.911
French. Le Louvre.

13:06.995 --> 13:10.331
- Please, let us hang up your coats.
- Oh, yes, thank you so much.

13:10.415 --> 13:12.125
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

13:12.208 --> 13:14.460
- Put 'em in there?
- Hang on. Hang on.

13:14.544 --> 13:18.006
- With the menu and everything.
- I know. It's impressive.

13:18.089 --> 13:19.132
Hi.

